ly use all available capacity, including empty requests with no available resources. I’ll remove that restriction and compare total demand against each resource’s capacity.","type":"output_text"}],"id":"msg_0c142b88638ddcfd016aecf92d39d887d2bd304b4abc513442","phase":"commentary","role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message"},{"arguments":"{\"content\":\"\\\"\\\"\\\"Check whether resource requests fit within available capacities.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n\\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Union\\n\\nNumber = Union[int, float]\\n\\n\\ndef is_allocation_feasible(\\n    resources: Dict[str, Number],\\n    requests: List[Dict[str, Number]]\\n) -> bool:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    Determine whether all requests can be satisfied given limited capacities.\\n\\n    Missing resources in a request require zero units. Unknown resource names\\n    make the allocation infeasible, even when the requested amount is zero.\\n    Exact capacity usage and empty request lists are feasible.\\n\\n    The inputs are assumed to contain nonnegative numeric capacities and amounts.\\n    Neither input is modified.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    totals = {resource: 0 for resource in resources}\\n\\n    for request in requests:\\n        for resource, amount in request.items():\\n            if resource not in resources:\\n                return False\\n            totals[resource] += amount\\n\\n    return all(totals[resource] <= capacity\\n               for resource, capacity in resources.items())\\n\",\"path\":\"src/solution.py\"}","call_id":"call_drGszzjXOPsCy319FH8Smsmu","id":"fc_0c142b88638ddcfd016aecf92e4cc887d2b06ad79ecb78c55c","name":"write_file","status":"completed","type":"function_call"},{"call_id":"call_drGszzjXOPsCy319FH8Smsmu","output":"{\"bytes\":1023,\"sha256\":\"5763771fcc3d1131070ffef1bc08329d251735ab50a1bcbb1035f8c824431e37\",\"status\":\"ok\"}\n","type":"function_call_output"},{"content":[],"encrypted_content":"gAAAAABq7PlQTiN3h0B91NYGvtI2uxyweeU-Ml8YaDdB1BSCmW6i7LCneU2g0zM6tOfeb6ElC